{:edb/db-before-t 1438 :edb/db-after-t 1439 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534751 50 #inst "2026-10-08T05:51:21.566Z" 13194139534751 true] [17592186128911 1100 "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139534751 true] [17592186128911 1100 "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534751 false] [17592186128911 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-2) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(5)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}.$" 13194139534751 true] [17592186128911 1145 "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I$:\n\n﻿﻿﻿$\\begin{bmatrix}1 - λ & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 - λ\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndet(A - λI) &= 0 \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 - λ & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 - λ\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\\\\n(1 - λ)(1 - λ) - 2(-2) &= 0 \\\\\n1 - 2λ + λ^{2} + 4 &= 0 \\\\\nλ^{2} - 2λ + 5 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-b ± \\sqrt{b^{2} - 4ac}}{2a} \\\\\n&= (- (-2) ± \\sqrt{(-2)^{2} - 4(1)(5)})/(2(1)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 ± \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 ± 4\\textrm{i}}{2} \\\\\n&= 1 ± 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n\\lambda=1\\pm 2\\textrm{i}\n$$" 13194139534751 false] [17592186128912 1100 "Given that $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ and $\\lambda_2$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $2(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2)$." 13194139534751 false] [17592186128912 1100 "Given that $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ and $\\lambda_2$ are eigenvalues of a real $2 \\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find $2(\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2).$" 13194139534751 true] [17592186128912 1145 "Since\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nis a complex eigenvalue of $A$, the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda_1$.\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda_2=\\overline{\\lambda}_1=-2-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(λ_{1} + λ_{2}) &= 2(-2 + 3\\textrm{i} + (-2 - 3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(-4) \\\\\n&=-8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534751 false] [17592186128912 1145 "Since $\\lambda_1=-2+3\\textrm{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of $\\lambda_1.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\lambda_2=\\overline{\\lambda}_1=-2-3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =2(-2+3\\text{i}+(-2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(-4) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534751 true] [17592186129093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307620 13194139534751 true] [17592186129093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307648 13194139534751 true] [17592186129093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307655 13194139534751 true] [17592186129093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307662 13194139534751 true] [17592186129093 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307683 13194139534751 true] [17592186129094 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307627 13194139534751 true] [17592186129094 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307634 13194139534751 true] [17592186129094 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307641 13194139534751 true] [17592186129094 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307669 13194139534751 true] [17592186129094 1020 #edb/ref 17592186307676 13194139534751 true] [17592186307620 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307621 1319413953475